    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1107">

                <pb facs="1293" n="1097" xml:id="pg1097"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/8–945</note>
                <head>No. 1107<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of
                        the Central Secretariat</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yost</hi>)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1107-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1107-f2"/>]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-09">August 9, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin Conference</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Italy</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Soviet Policy</hi></p>
                <p>. . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>On two occasions the Soviets presented proposals in regard to the imposition of
                    reparations on Italy.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1107-f3"/> The United States and
                    Britain refused to agree except in the case of delivery of capital equipment
                    from war industries having no peacetime utility. No decision was taken on this
                    matter.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">British Policy</hi></p>
                <p>… On reparations he<anchor n="4" xml:id="d1107-f4"/> said that the British did
                    not wish them for themselves but were thinking of Greece.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>… They<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1107-f5"/> also strongly supported the United States
                    position on Italian reparations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1107-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1107-f1-content">
                <p>Printed from the ribbon copy, which is unsigned. For the minutes of the
                    discussions summarized in this memorandum, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg55">pp. 55</ref>, <ref target="#pg174"
                        >174</ref>–<ref target="#pg175">175</ref>, <ref target="#pg323">323</ref>,
                        <ref target="#pg464">464</ref>–<ref target="#pg465">465</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg482">482</ref>, <ref target="#pg484">484</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1107-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1107-f2-content">
                <p>For the other sections of this memorandum, see <ref target="#d738">documents Nos.
                        738</ref> and <ref target="#d1093">1093</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1107-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1107-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d1099">Documents Nos. 1099</ref> and <ref target="#d1104"
                        >1104</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1107-f4" n="4" xml:id="d1107-f4-content">
                <p>i. e., Churchill.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1107-f5" n="5" xml:id="d1107-f5-content">
                <p>i. e., Attlee and Bevin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
